course: dictionary
lesson: 14492
title: Payer and taxpayer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A payer is the person or group who pays money. The word comes from the verb to pay, so the payer is the one who hands over the money. When Mum buys lunch, she is the payer.
explain: Context clues help you spot a payer. Look for words like bill, cost, money or price. «In the shop, Mum was the payer for our lunch.» The word payer names the one who gave the money.
explain: A taxpayer is a person who pays taxes. Taxes are money that people pay to the government. «Every taxpayer helps pay for schools and hospitals.» Taxpayer is a special kind of payer, with the word tax inside it.
explain: In a maths story about buying or bills, the payer is the one who gives the money. Ask yourself: who hands over the money? That person is the payer.
fact: A payer is the person or group who pays money.
fact: «Payer» is a noun, and its plural is «payers».
fact: A taxpayer is a person who pays taxes.
fact: In a bill story, the payer is the one who gives the money.
fact: A good check is to ask who hands over the money, then swap in the word payer to see if it makes sense.
exercise: «Mum was the payer for our lunch, so she gave the cashier the money.» Who is the payer? | The cashier | The table | The lunch | *Mum
exercise: In a maths story, «Ten children bought tickets, and Ben was the payer.» What is the payer in this story? | The one who sells the tickets | The one who counts the children | The one who has the most tickets | *The one who pays the money for the tickets
exercise: Which word is the plural of payer? | payer's | *payers | payed | paying
test: «Every taxpayer helps to pay for schools and hospitals.» What is a taxpayer? | The school teacher who works at the hospital | A doctor in a hospital | *A person who pays taxes | A person who sells taxes
test: «Four friends ate pizza, and Sam was the payer for the whole bill.» Who is the payer? | The pizza | *Sam | Nobody, because the bill was free | The waiter
exam: Which word means a person who pays taxes? | payer | taxi | *taxpayer | tax
